    "description": "Original MCQs for a Bavaria-specific exam-prep module for the German Fischerprüfung / Fischereischein (Angelschein) in the Free State of Bavaria, covering species-specific closed seasons and minimum sizes (Schonzeiten/Mindestmaße, Anlage to §11 AVBayFiG, including the river-basin-scoped rules for certain species), Bavaria-specific gear and method rules (prohibited devices/methods under §15 AVBayFiG, hand-rod hook-count and supervision rules under §16 AVBayFiG), the Bavarian Fischereischein/Fischerprüfung process (Art. 46-50 BayFiG license duty, age rules incl. the 1 Jan 2025 abolition of the separate Jugendfischereischein, exam subject areas and format under Art. 48 BayFiG / §4-§5 AVBayFiG), general fish biology and species identification for fish found in Bavarian waters, and Bavaria-specific water/nature protection and fisheries-law context (Hegepflicht and sustainability principle under Art. 1 BayFiG, geschlossene Gewässer under Art. 2 BayFiG, fishing-rights ownership under Art. 3 BayFiG, Gewässerrandstreifen under Art. 21 BayWG, fisheries-warden enforcement, catch-and-release and stocking rules under AVBayFiG). Content is independently phrased and grounded directly in BayFiG and AVBayFiG statute/regulation text (gesetze-bayern.de Bürgerservice; AVBayFiG version in force from 1 June 2025 as mirrored by a Bavarian fisheries cooperative's member service) and BayWG statute text, cross-checked against summaries published by the Landesfischereiverband Bayern / Fischereiverband Oberbayern and a local angling club, NOT sourced or paraphrased from the official LfL Bayern Fragenkatalog (https://www.lfl.bayern.de/mam/cms07/ifi/dateien/fragenkatalog_2023-endversion.pdf) or from any commercial exam-prep catalog. This is a fully independent exam module - separate content pool and exam simulation from the existing generic 'angelschein' module and from every other module in this app; it is Bavaria-specific and does not aim to cover other German states' Fischereigesetze.",
    "class": "ALL",
